<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/3rd-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Red Cliffs</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">208</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a> · Also known as Battle of Chibi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Red Cliffs was fought on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yangtze-river">Yangtze</a> in the winter of 208–209, at the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-dynasty">Han dynasty</a>. The allied forces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sun-quan">Sun Quan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liu-bei">Liu Bei</a>, led by Zhou Yu, defeated the much larger army of the northern warlord <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cao-cao">Cao Cao</a>, partly through fire ships. It stopped Cao Cao's advance south and led to the division of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/three-kingdoms-period">Three Kingdoms</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-red-cliffs.jpg" alt="Battle of Red Cliffs" width="320" height="270" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User Jie on en.wikipedia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chibi.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
